    },
    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_basis_treatment_response",
      "value": "used",
      "quote": "Clonazepam was added and the dose gradually increased to 4 mg/d. There was a slight reduction in the number of spasms, but the axial stiffness and the hyperlordosis of the lumbar spine persisted. She was unable to tolerate higher doses of clonazepam because of drowsiness, and in December 1995, vigabatrin was re-started at a dose of 0.5 g/d and increased to 2 g/d. When reviewed in January 1996, the spasms had ceased and there was almost complete resolution of the axial stiffness and the hyperlordosis of the lumbar spine.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
